# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12 (Q45 and its additions): a unit-level method executes Counter natively --
# a call of its procedure, the pair (its occurrence, Counter) through lmx_call_prim -- and Counter's body
# runs as a method's: while counts 5, the if adds 2, the for 3, put adds 4 to seen, and the return in a
# block ends it before `n: 100U`.  run executes it twice and reads n: 10 (its declaration runs again);
# seen 8.  Entry 7.
size_t: seen 0U
fn: put (size_t: a) int
    seen: seen + a
return: 0
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    size_t: k 0U
    while: k < 5U
        n: n + 1U
        k: k + 1U
    if: n = 5U
        n: n + 2U
    else:
        n: 100U
    for: int(i, 0) (i < 3) i++
        n: n + 1U
    end: for
    put: 4U
    if: n = 10U
        return
    n: 100U
return
fn: run () size_t
    Counter
    Counter
    size_t: v 9U
    v: Counter\n
return: v
size_t: got 9U
got: run()
int: ok 0
if: got = 10U && seen = 8U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
